# Bytes as a signed 32-bit integer `i32`: a 4-byte chain reinterpreted
# as two's complement. For any other length the `cant-convert` fallback
# takes an error message. When unbound, it terminates with that message.

+architect yegor256@gmail.com
+home https://github.com/objectionary/eo
+package bytes
+spdx SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright (c) 2016-2026 Objectionary.com
+spdx SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
+unlint invalid-name-notation
+version 0.0.0

[^data cant-convert] > as-i32
  if. > @
    data.size.eq 4
    i32 data
    cant-convert
      "Can't convert non 4 length bytes to i32, bytes are %x".printf
        * data

  00-00-00-33.as-i32.as-bytes.eq 00-00-00-33 ++> can-convert-bytes-to-i32-and-back

  eq. ++> can-recover-from-bytes-of-wrong-size-when-converting-to-i32
    i32 FF-FE-4C-17
    03-5A-E1.as-i32
      i32 FF-FE-4C-17 > [message]

  01-01-01-01-01.as-i32 --> stops-on-bytes-of-wrong-size-when-converting-to-i32
